---
import BaseLayout from '@/components/layout/BaseLayout.astro';
import ProcessTimeline from '@/components/process/ProcessTimeline.astro';

const analyticalSteps = [
  {
    number: '1',
    title: 'Define the analytical object',
    body: 'Clarify what the analysis is supposed to measure before choosing a method. In the fiscal vulnerability project, the object is not local revenue but the combination of fiscal potential and fiscal effort.'
  },
  {
    number: '2',
    title: 'Build reliable data before modelling',
    body: 'Prepare the data layer through ingestion, schema normalization, variable mapping, missing-value handling and validation checks, especially when public datasets change over time.'
  },
  {
    number: '3',
    title: 'Choose methods that match the question',
    body: 'Use regression, machine learning, scoring, network analysis, input-output modelling or visual exploration depending on whether the question is causal, predictive, structural, territorial or systemic.'
  },
  {
    number: '4',
    title: 'Make results auditable and communicable',
    body: 'Keep source data, transformations, indicators, diagnostics, outputs and interpretation separable so results can be checked, reused and explained clearly.'
  }
];

const toolGroups = [
  {
    title: 'Programming and notebooks',
    tools: ['Python', 'R', 'Marimo', 'Jupyter', 'Google Apps Script']
  },
  {
    title: 'Data manipulation',
    tools: ['pandas', 'NumPy', 'pyarrow', 'DuckDB', 'Excel', 'Power Query']
  },
  {
    title: 'Databases and SQL',
    tools: ['SQL', 'PostgreSQL', 'BigQuery', 'DuckDB SQL']
  },
  {
    title: 'Visualisation and BI',
    tools: ['Power BI', 'Tableau', 'Altair', 'Matplotlib', 'Plotly']
  },
  {
    title: 'Modelling and statistics',
    tools: ['Regression', 'PPML', 'Difference-in-difference', 'Gradient Boosting', 'Random Forest', 'Cross-validation']
  },
  {
    title: 'Workflow and reproducibility',
    tools: ['Git', 'pytest', 'Parquet', 'Schema validation', 'Data-quality diagnostics']
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title="Analytical Approach | Yannis Daguenet">
  <section class="methods-section">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Methods</p>
      <h1>Analytical Approach</h1>

      <p class="hero-text">
        My work usually starts from a policy or economic question that is too broad to analyse directly. The first step is to turn that question into a measurable analytical object: a fiscal vulnerability score, a trade shock estimate, a carbon-flow network, a prediction target, or a transition pathway.
      </p>

      <p class="hero-text">
        The common thread across the portfolio is not one single method, but multiple depending on the needs of the project.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="methods-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <h2>How the analytical process connects</h2>
        <p>
          Across projects, the workflow is not linear in a mechanical sense, but the same logic returns: define the object, build reliable data, choose the method, then make the result auditable and communicable.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ProcessTimeline steps={analyticalSteps} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="method-cards-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="container-narrow method-cards-header">
        <h2>Methods used across the portfolio</h2>
        <p>
          These methods are not used as a fixed checklist. They are selected depending on what the project needs to measure, explain, predict, or communicate.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="method-grid">
        <article class="method-card">
          <h3>Data pipelines</h3>
          <p>
            Ingestion, cleaning, schema normalization, Parquet conversion, validation, and reproducible data preparation.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="method-card">
          <h3>Statistical analysis</h3>
          <p>
            Exploratory analysis, regression, difference-in-difference, PPML, diagnostics, and robustness-oriented interpretation.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="method-card">
          <h3>Machine learning</h3>
          <p>
            Feature engineering, imputation, model benchmarking, cross-validation, and predictive interpretation.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="method-card">
          <h3>Network and systems analysis</h3>
          <p>
            Input-output networks, embodied carbon flows, centrality, phase-space trajectories, and agent-based modelling.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="method-card">
          <h3>Policy interpretation</h3>
          <p>
            Translation of analytical results into concise explanations, limitations, and decision-relevant findings.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="method-card">
          <h3>Visual communication</h3>
          <p>
            Finding-based titles, readable charts, direct captions, and visual choices tied to the analytical question.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

    <section class="tools-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="container-narrow tools-header">
        <h2>Tools used across the portfolio</h2>
        <p>
          The portfolio combines analytical programming, data engineering, statistical modelling, visualisation, and reproducible workflow tools. The tools vary by project, but they are used to support the same objective: turning complex data into interpretable results.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="tools-grid">
        {toolGroups.map((group) => (
          <article class="tool-group">
            <h3>{group.title}</h3>
            <div class="tool-list">
              {group.tools.map((tool) => (
                <span>{tool}</span>
              ))}
            </div>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .methods-section,
  .method-cards-section {
    padding: var(--space-3xl) 0;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-lg);
    font-size: var(--font-size-4xl);
    line-height: 1.05;
  }

  .hero-text,
  .methods-section p,
  .method-cards-header p {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .method-cards-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .method-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .method-card {
    background-color: var(--color-panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .method-card h3 {
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .method-card p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

    .tools-section {
    padding: var(--space-3xl) 0;
  }

  .tools-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .tools-header p {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .tools-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .tool-group {
    background-color: var(--color-panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .tool-group h3 {
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .tool-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .tool-list span {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background-color: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .methods-section,
    .method-cards-section,
    .tools-section {
      padding: var(--space-2xl) 0;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: var(--font-size-3xl);
    }

    .method-grid,
    .tools-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>